223	238	nexus/correctness-require-blocking-standard-streams	exitBeforeBlockingStandardStreams	This file runs as a process (nothing in the program imports it), and this `process.exit()` runs after a write to stdout or stderr before the process has called `blockStandardStreams()`. Node writes to a pipe asynchronously, and `process.exit()` does not wait: a reader piping this process gets the output cut off (measured: 65,536 of 1 MiB), with exit status 0 and no error. Call Nexus's `blockStandardStreams()` (`source/system/StandardStreams`) before anything that can exit: first in the module, or first in the main it runs.	0	0
